8.1 — The Governance Principle: No Agent Contradicts Another
The architectural breakthrough that separates KEYSTONE from all competing approaches is governance. In a standard multi-agent environment, each agent maintains its own context independently. Over time — over many sessions, many clients, many workflows — agents develop divergent understandings of who they work for, what the priorities are, and what the right outputs look like. The result is output inconsistency: the Outlook agent drafts emails in one tone, the content agent posts in another, the proposal agent uses pricing logic that no longer reflects AX's current model. The agents are technically functioning — but they are not coordinated. They are a collection of isolated tools, not a workforce.
In the KEYSTONE dome, the Eternal Seed is the single source of truth. Every agent reads from it at session start. No agent can develop independent context that contradicts the Seed. When the Seed is updated — monthly, or when a significant decision is made — all agents inherit the update simultaneously. The dome maintains coherence at scale. A 30-client KEYSTONE operation with 7 active agents is as coordinated on day 365 as it was on day 1, because every agent has always drawn from the same truth.
8.2 — The Session Log Architecture
Every automated action taken by every node is recorded in an append-only SharePoint log — timestamped, categorized by node and venture, and tagged by client if applicable. This log serves three functions: it gives AX complete visibility into what the dome is doing without requiring supervision; it provides the raw material for the monthly Eternal Seed update (the delta between this month's log and last month's is what the Seed needs to know); and it creates an audit trail for any action that a client or legal party might later question.
The session log is the dome's memory. The Eternal Seed is the dome's intelligence. Together, they make the automation system not just faster than a human team — but more organized, more consistent, and more accountable.

