Power Automate is the orchestration backbone of the KEYSTONE dome. It is the layer that connects events to actions, triggers to workflows, and nodes to each other. The following 8 flows represent the complete Phase 2 and Phase 3 build priority. Each flow is described with its trigger, its logic chain, and its role in the dome.

FLOW 1 — New Email to Lead Score
Trigger: Email received in designated intake folder. Logic: GPT analysis via Copilot Studio API reads email body → scores lead on KEYSTONE fit rubric (revenue, industry, tool stack, urgency, geography) → routes HIGH fit to intake agent, MEDIUM fit to holding queue, LOW fit to polite decline template. AX sees only HIGH and MEDIUM leads. Time from email receipt to lead score: 90 seconds.


FLOW 2 — Signed Contract to Onboarding
Trigger: E-signature webhook fires (DocuSign or Adobe Sign). Logic: Signature confirmed → delivery agent triggered → client added to KEYSTONE roster in SharePoint → onboarding questionnaire sent via Outlook → calendar holds set for onboarding session → Stripe payment link generated → invoice sent. From signature to fully initiated onboarding: 5 minutes, zero human steps.


FLOW 3 — Monthly Eternal Seed Update
Trigger: 1st of month, 9:00 AM. Logic: Pull all session logs from SharePoint for the past 30 days → identify deltas (new clients, resolved decisions, changed priorities, new ventures) → generate Eternal Seed update draft in the correct schema → send to AX for review with tracked changes format. AX approves, declines sections, or edits. Approved update is written back to the Seed file. All agents inherit the update at next session start.


FLOW 4 — Invoice to Payment to Receipt
Trigger: Invoice generated event (from Flow 2 or monthly billing cycle). Logic: Invoice formatted and sent via Outlook → Stripe payment link embedded → payment received webhook fires → receipt generated and sent automatically → revenue dashboard updated in Excel via Node 3 → session log entry created. The entire billing lifecycle is zero-touch for AX.


FLOW 5 — Lead to Proposal Pipeline
Trigger: Intake form completed (KEYSTONE or Axes Contracting). Logic: Form responses extracted → Node 2 generates proposal using Axes Contracting template + seed context → proposal sent to AX approval queue with one-click send button → if approved, proposal sent to prospect → if not responded in 48 hours, follow-up drafted → if not responded in 7 days, final follow-up sent with expiration notice. AX's single action: click approve.


FLOW 6 — Content Calendar Engine
Trigger: Sunday 8:00 PM weekly. Logic: Node 6 pulls weekly KEYSTONE priorities from Eternal Seed → drafts 5 LinkedIn posts (Mon–Fri) in AX's voice → drafts 1 long-form article → queues all 6 pieces in SharePoint content calendar → sends AX a 20-minute Monday review request → approved posts scheduled for auto-publish → declined posts revised with AI note and re-queued for next cycle.


FLOW 7 — Churn Alert and Re-Engagement
Trigger: Daily 7:00 AM check. Logic: For every active KEYSTONE client, calculate days since last engagement (email, session, or document) → if >21 days, escalate to yellow alert → if >30 days, generate red churn alert for AX → draft re-engagement email in AX's voice referencing the client's specific seed content (their ventures, their priorities) → hold for AX approval → if AX approves and client still unresponsive after 7 more days, escalate to strategic discussion flag.


FLOW 8 — Daily Briefing Assembly
Trigger: 7:45 AM daily. Logic: Pull all pending approvals from SharePoint queue → pull today's calendar from Outlook → pull any churn alerts from Flow 7 → pull any financial anomalies from Node 3 → pull KEYSTONE priorities from Eternal Seed → assemble into structured daily briefing template → deliver via Teams chat message at 8:00 AM sharp. The briefing is AX's command center for the day — everything that needs attention, prioritized, with one-click actions where possible.


